+# Design: authored Markdown → knowledge bundle
+
+## Goal
+Turn authored Markdown documents into a `KnowledgeBundle` (knowledge-bundle/v1) so they can go
+through the existing bundle import unchanged. The result is deterministic.
+
+## Scope
+Included: new module `pharma_agent.domain.corpus.authoring` (pure domain, no IO).
+Unchanged: `bundle.py`, models, import service, DB, API. No new dependencies.
+
+## Interfaces
+```python
+@dataclass(frozen=True) class MarkdownSection: heading: str; path: tuple[str, ...]; ordinal: int; blocks: list[BlockRecord]
+@dataclass(frozen=True) class AuthoredDocument: key: str; title: str; markdown: str
+def split_markdown(markdown: str, *, fallback_heading: str) -> list[MarkdownSection]
+def slugify(text: str, *, max_length: int = 80) -> str
+def section_key(document_key: str, path: Sequence[str]) -> str
+def section_choices(collection: BundleCollection, documents: Sequence[AuthoredDocument]) -> list[tuple[str, str]]
+def build_bundle(collection: BundleCollection, documents: Sequence[AuthoredDocument],
+                 glossary: Sequence[GlossaryEntry], colloquial: Sequence[ColloquialMappingRecord]) -> KnowledgeBundle
+```
+
+## Approach
+- `split_markdown`: line scan; ``` / ~~~ fences toggle a flag so `#` lines inside are text. ATX headings
+  (`#`..`######`) start a section; `path` is the stack of enclosing headings including the heading itself
+  (empty for the pre-heading section). Text before the first heading, or a headingless document, is a
+  section titled `fallback_heading` with empty path. Sections without content are dropped; ordinals are
+  0-based over kept sections.
+- Blocks: within a section, runs of lines starting with `|` (outside fences) become one TABLE block with
+  `table_key` `t1`, `t2`… counted across the document; other text between is stripped PROSE (blank-only
+  dropped).
+- `slugify`: NFD-normalise, `đ`→`d`, drop marks, lowercase, non-alnum runs → `-`, trim, cut to max_length
+  (re-trim hyphen).
+- `section_key`: `<doc>#<slugs joined by "/">`, `<doc>#body` if path empty. Duplicate keys in one document
+  (same slugged path) get `-2`, `-3` suffixes so keys stay unique; empty slugs become `section`.
+- Bundle document key = `<collection.key>:<doc.key>`. Documents sorted by that key; `section_choices` and
+  `build_bundle` share one internal generator so keys and order agree. Label = title › path parts (fallback
+  heading for body sections is not added: the label is just the title).
+- `build_bundle`: DocumentKind.GENERAL_MONOGRAPH, SourceInfo(title). Colloquial section keys not present are
+  filtered out. Manifest: collection, fixed generator `pharma-agent-authoring`/`1`/`authoring`, empty
+  source_digests, counts, `files={}` (as `write_bundle` computes digests). No timestamps/randomness.
+
+## Testing
+`tests/domain/corpus/test_authoring.py`: splitting (fences, preamble, no headings, empty sections, tables,
+numbering across sections), slugify, section_key, choices, build_bundle (sorting, key prefixing, filtering,
+manifest counts, determinism via `write_bundle` file digests, validity via `write_bundle`/`read_bundle`).
